{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Please sit, I will check the pressure and the weight before you go in. The machine is slow only today.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. We were stuck near the metro, amma was scolding the auto fellow the whole way, and I have a class at four so I am a bit rushed.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Today the blood pressure is 118 over 74, pulse is 78. Weight flashed 71, uh ignore that, it has settled at 67.5 kg.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): In the camp last time they said higher, I don't remember the figure. Is doctor free?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Yes, go in. I have put 118/74 and 67.5 on the slip.",
  "[SEG0006] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sorry, err, one second. The screen is just loading. Mm. Right. What is the problem?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Ma'am the pimples, and periods are not coming proper. It has been one year... no, sorry, two years, since I entered second year college.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (DOCTOR): Two years, acne and irregular periods. How often are the periods coming? Say again, the cursor jumped.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Once in three months, sometimes four months. The last one was just before my cousin's wedding, and that function, what to say, the lehenga fitting was a whole drama.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): Okay, leave the wedding. Any fever?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any cough, or trouble breathing? Anything chest wise?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Chest is completely fine, no cough also.",
  "[SEG0014] person_4 (DOCTOR): Headaches? Giddiness?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): No headache, and no giddiness.",
  "[SEG0016] person_4 (DOCTOR): What about appetite?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm that one is mixed. Some days I am very hungry, some days I leave half the plate, I cannot say if it is more or less.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She has put on weight, and hairs are coming on the chin. I told her not to thread every week.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes. I was thinking five kilos, no, it is eight kilos, the old jeans are proof. And the hair on the chin and the sideburns, that started since Diwali or after, I cannot place the date.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (DOCTOR): Eight kilos, not five. I noted that. The Diwali part, you are not sure. When did the weight itself start going up?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): That also I cannot date. Last winter, or the one before. My memory for months is hopeless.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): Are you on any tablets or creams now? This page is blank, tell me again.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): I was putting clindamycin gel... uh no, not clindamycin, it was adapaline, 0.1 percent, at night. Maybe six weeks, then I stopped, the skin was burning. My cousin takes metformin, I never took that.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I have diabetes since ten years, on tablets. Her nani also had sugar. But this girl, no tablets from our side.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (DOCTOR): Okay, adapalene stopped, not the clindamycin. Let me see. Acne on both cheeks and on the chin, and a few coarse hairs on the chin. The neck is clear, no dark thickening.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): The burning from that gel is gone now. In college people ask if I did some facial, it is so embarrassing, and the canteen samosa is too good, that is half my problem.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (DOCTOR): I am thinking this may be polycystic ovary syndrome, from the acne, the irregular cycles, the chin hair and the weight. Only a working impression, not a confirmed diagnosis.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Is it because of my sugar? Will she also get diabetes?",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (DOCTOR): Not necessarily from you. I am booking bloods, the sugar and the hormones, and a pelvic ultrasound. Kindly do both before you come back.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Ultrasound, like for pregnancy? I am not married ma'am, will they even do it, and does it hurt?",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (DOCTOR): It is only a pelvic scan, nothing to do with pregnancy, and it should not hurt. The combined contraceptive pill can settle cycles and acne, but I am not starting it today. We might consider it only if the bloods look suitable.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): My friend started a pill and she had nausea the whole month, so I got scared only.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fair enough. For now, cut the sweets and the samosa, and walk thirty minutes most days. Come back in four weeks with the reports. Sorry, the weight gain figure again, the typing lagged.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Eight kilos. I will cut the samosa and try the walking. The dates I still cannot pin, Diwali or after, and the winter thing, same confusion.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I will bring her for the tests. I will remind her to walk, though I myself skip it most days.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): Good. Take the forms from reception on the way out."
 ],
